        <item>
            <title>1.13.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:04:51 +0530</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>227</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.13.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li>Fixed: when two downloads started together, one app&#x27;s progress could show in another&#x27;s row, the bar jumped back and forth, and one download never finished (Cancel couldn&#x27;t stop it either). Each download now keeps to its own row, and the bar only moves forward.</li>
  <li>A download never sits silently: the row says &quot;Connecting…&quot; until data arrives, a download that gets nothing for a minute starts once more on its own, and if it stalls again the row says so and the run carries on.</li>
  <li>Homebrew apps download up to three at once and then install one at a time, and Homebrew and App Store updates now run side by side.</li>
  <li>Keel keeps a short log of each download in ~/Library/Logs/Keel/updates.log (7 days).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
